    <!-- lameta-source {"folderType":"session","folderId":"INT_2022_0747","fieldKey":"description"} -->
    <Description>Tenzin Yılmaz talks about triangles as a form of apology. The artist brought a canvas, unwrapped it, looked at it, and wrapped it again.</Description>
